## DESKTOP EDITOR LAYOUT

Use a sophisticated, fixed-height workspace.

The overall editor should fit the available browser viewport.

Avoid page-level vertical scrolling in the editor.

Use the following layout:

TOP HEADER:
- Back to Collections.
- Current template category and name.
- Santa Studio branding.
- Optional Save Draft indicator.

MAIN WORKSPACE:

LEFT PANEL — CUSTOMISATION FORM

RIGHT PANEL — LIVE CARD PREVIEW

BOTTOM OF RIGHT PANEL — TEMPLATE SELECTOR

BOTTOM ACTION BAR:
- Preview.
- Download PNG.

### Important layout rules

The left form and right preview must start at the same vertical position.

The preview must remain visible while the user edits the form.

Only the form panel may scroll independently if the form exceeds available height.

The action bar must always remain visible.

The customer should never need to scroll to the top to view their card again.

The preview should automatically scale according to available space.

The template selector must be horizontal and independently scrollable.

Do not use global overflow:hidden in a way that clips the page header, footer or content.

Use CSS Grid and min-height: 0 correctly.

